            <ArticleTitle>Effect of biphasic endocardial countershock on pacing thresholds in humans.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>527-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The use of non-thoracotomy endocardial implantable defibrillators with pacing capabilities has increased substantially over the past 2 years. This report demonstrates that the pacing threshold increases in some patients after endocardial defibrillation, and substantiates the practice of using maximal pacing output after endocardial defibrillation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
